{"kind": "mod", "id": 1421, "name": "Crysis 2 Music Pack", "slug": "crysis-2-music-pack", "teaser": "Hans Zimmer, Lorne Balfe, Borislav Slavov and Tilman Sillescu will be taking over your main menu's music.", "owner_name": "totallyjon", "downloads": 844, "favourites": 0, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": null, "guid": null, "thumbnail_local": null, "category": null, "category_id": null, "updated_at": "2026-07-07T16:58:56.000000Z", "created_at": "2024-05-19T14:43:08.000000Z", "published_at": "2024-05-19T14:43:08.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~3.8.0", "latest_version": "1.0.0", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": null, "description_html": "<p><strong>1) Drop CustomMusic in BepInEx/plugins.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>2) When in-game, open your F12 menu and find CustomMusicPlayer. By default, it loads 5 songs. Set this to 46 so that it pulls music from the entire soundtrack.</strong></p>\n<p>I took Junko Space Mommy’s <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1832-stalker-music-pack/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">STALKER Music Pack</a> and replaced its contents with Crysis 2’s soundtrack. I recommend using <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1922-raid-movie-background-replacer/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Raid Movie Background Replacer</a> with this music replacement mod for that “cool” feeling because it goes very well together.</p>\n<div class=\"youtube-lite\" data-video-id=\"yr481EULIcE\" data-embed-url=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/yr481EULIcE?autoplay=1\"><img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yr481EULIcE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"YouTube video thumbnail\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" /></div>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.0.0", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.8.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 844, "published_at": "2024-05-19T14:43:08.000000Z", "forge